{# Partial template — HTML-producing reusable component.
   See logic-engine/rules/partials.md for the rules this template enforces:
   - partials-no-underscore-prefix: filename must not start with _
   - render-vs-function-tags: render for HTML output, function for data
   - graphql-in-partials-restricted: only data-heavy block partials may have GraphQL

   Params:
     name              — partial name (without leading _ or .liquid)
     params            — array of expected parameter names (documented at top)
     allows_graphql    — boolean. If true, partial is a data-heavy block; otherwise pure presentation.
#}
{% comment %}
  Partial: <%= it.name %>
  Expected parameters:
<% if (it.params && it.params.length > 0) { -%>
<% it.params.forEach(function(p) { -%>
    - <%= p %>
<% }) -%>
<% } else { -%>
    (none)
<% } -%>

  Rules:
  - Pure presentation: no GraphQL, no state changes. Receive data as parameters from the caller.
<% if (!it.allows_graphql) { -%>
  - This partial is marked as pure presentation. Do not add {% graphql %} blocks.
<% } -%>
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} TODO: partial body. {% endcomment %}
